{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794987670,"nonce":"pata8awmLn3roHBsn6j5TfJmh/k=","title":"[GitHub #84] Alt+letter is delivered as text input to a focused text field","message":"Source: https://github.com/project-blinc/Blinc/issues/84\nReporter: FreeSynergy\nGitHub state at capture: open\nReported: 2026-11-17T01:56:04Z; updated: 2026-11-17T01:56:04Z\nCaptured: 2026-11-18T07:38:25.958Z\n\nStatus: queued from the upstream report. This import does not claim local reproduction, implementation or a fix.\n\nTracking scope and expected outcome\n\nPrevent handled Alt+letter menu mnemonics from inserting text before the shortcut runs. Review KEY_DOWN versus TEXT_INPUT ordering and modifier handling. Preserve ordinary typing, Ctrl/Meta shortcuts, layout-aware text from merged PR #73, AltGr/Option text entry and IME composition. The original headless reproduction does not establish native text delivery on X11/Wayland/macOS/Windows; validate those paths rather than suppressing all Alt text.\n\nOriginal GitHub report\n\nHello, and thank you for Blinc.\n\nA key chord such as Alt+F, which a menu bar uses as a mnemonic, is not excluded from text input: the letter is inserted into a focused text field, and the shortcut handler sees the chord only after the character.\n\nCheck, run against cf925af (fs-blinc-3.1):\n\nThe test feeds the same event sequence the window produces into a real Blinc text input (the TextInput widget inside a small dialog) and into an on_key_down hook on the root element. For a key press with a character the window sends TEXT_INPUT first, then KEY_DOWN; the only chords left out of TEXT_INPUT are Ctrl without AltGr, and Meta.\n\nResult at cf925af:\n- Alt+F (character 'f', code 70, alt = true): the text field now contains \"f\". The hook sees (code 70, alt = true) only after the character is already in the field.\n- Ctrl+F and Meta+F: nothing is typed, the hook sees both presses.\n- Plain F: \"f\" is typed (control case).\n\nWhere the behaviour comes from:\n- crates/blinc_app/src/windowed/event_loop/input/keyboard.rs:244-259 (cf925af) builds TEXT_INPUT unless Ctrl (without AltGr) or Meta is held; Alt is not tested. On project-blinc/Blinc main (67f54d2) the same condition is at :238-251 (`if !mods.ctrl \u0026\u0026 !mods.meta`).\n- crates/blinc_layout/src/widgets/text_input/handlers.rs:373 and crates/blinc_layout/src/widgets/text_area/handlers.rs:250-251 skip TEXT_INPUT only for ctx.ctrl or ctx.meta; ctx.alt is never read (identical on cf925af and main).\n\nWhat the test does not show: whether winit delivers text for Alt+letter on Windows or macOS. At cf925af the character comes from the platform text (keyboard.rs:84-85); on main it comes from the key itself (keyboard.rs:82), so Alt+F gives 'f' there on every platform. We expect the platform text for Alt+F to be \"f\" on X11 and Wayland but have not measured it, and we have not run it on Windows or macOS.\n\nWhy it matters: a menu bar that opens with Alt+F (mnemonic) inserts an \"f\" into a focused text field, and the shortcut handler runs after the character.\n\nThe test is a plain cargo test (no window): fs-components-widgets/tests/alt_letter_spike.rs in the branch unreviewed/components-menue-m2 of FreeSynergy/fs-components (commit d08bdbb9). It uses the public broadcast_text_input_event and broadcast_key_event of RenderTree. Test names: alt_letter_is_typed_into_the_field_and_reaches_the_hook_after_it, ctrl_and_meta_letters_are_not_typed, a_plain_letter_is_typed.\n\nAlso tracked in git-bug in our fork FreeSynergy/Blinc (id ec7815a).","files":null}]}